Computer simulations only tell half the story. When engineers bolt **SAPPHIRE CRYSTAL TO TITANIUM DIFFUSION BONDING** onto a test bench and film it under full load with high-speed cameras and laser sensors, real-world flex and microscopic slip show up immediately.

{{ FIGURE_0 }}

During the first few milliseconds of startup, mating surfaces settle into contact before reaching steady-state operation—which is why break-in surface finish matters so much.
